BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
UID:69a85b71b48451fc3c069f76@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Romance Book Club\, where love stories take cen
 ter stage and every page promises a new adventure of the heart. Whether yo
 u're into slow burns\, second chances\, or enemies-to-lovers\, there's som
 ething here for every kind of romantic. Come read\, swoon\, and share your
  favorite moments with fellow book lovers.\nThe Romance Book Club title fo
 r Saturday June 13 2026 is\nProblematic Summer Romance\nby Ali Hazelwood.
 \nPlease note that this book club is for individuals 18+.\nLimited copies 
 will be available in branch for pick up.\nDrop in\, no registration requir
 ed.\nThis program was previously scheduled for June 6 and has been re-sche
 duled to June 13.
LOCATION:Maryvale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a85b71b48451fc3c069f76
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scrabble Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T153000
UID:69e16419b6c4ac1fedccea6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Put your word skills to the test! Join us for some friendly Sc
 rabble in a relaxed\, welcoming space. Whether you are a triple-word-score
  pro or new to the game\, all adults are welcome.\nDrop-in\, no registrati
 on required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e16419b6c4ac1fedccea6d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Container Gardening with Toronto Master Gardeners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
UID:6a21f64d52c88111723d0f39@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Apartment\, condominium and townhouse dwellers deserve to have
  beautiful and bountiful outdoor gardens too! Join a Toronto Master Garden
 er to learn practical tricks for successful gardening “above ground”\,
  taking into account your special challenges\, share design ideas\, and re
 commend plant choices\, including annuals\, perennials\, bulbs\, shrubs\, 
 trees\, edibles and native plants.\nDrop-in.\n**Subject to change. Please 
 visit the site periodically for updates to this posting**\nThe program wil
 l take place in the Auditorium located in the basement. Elevator on site. 
 If you have any questions\, please call Bendale Branch at 416-396-8910.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Auditorium - Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21f64d52c88111723d0f39
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Game Night: Catan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T193000
UID:69a896f02866a5b4883fe67a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening of fun\, games\, learning\, and communi
 ty.\nFrom games of strategy to games of chance\, all levels of experience 
 are welcome.\nPlease note the program has had some changes. Previously\, i
 t was Charades but is now Catan.\nPlease note date change for program. Pre
 viously scheduled for Wednesday June 10 and re-scheduled to Tuesday June 9
 .\nDrop-in. No registration required. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Maryvale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a896f02866a5b4883fe67a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
