BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board Games for Adults: Wednesday Afternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T160000
UID:69a204c61e64afd01e5e9197@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the fun of playing modern and classic board games!
 \nDrop in with your friends (or make some new ones) and play games like:\n
 Anomia\, Backgammon\, Bananagrams\, Chess\, CodeNames\, Connect Four\, Ex
 ploding Kittens\, Monopoly\, Quirkle\, Rumikub\, Scrabble\, Set\, Settlers
  of Catan\, Snakes and Ladders\, Sorry\, SushiGO\, UNO\, UpWords and ma
 ny more!\nPlease don't hesitate to call us or visit the red desk on the fi
 rst floor if you have any questions.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a204c61e64afd01e5e9197
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T170000
UID:6a1ede64703c3363002bb5d5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by the\nToronto Em
 ergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in partnership with
  the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:\nThe potential
  hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to 
 assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networks d
 uring emergencies\nFree program.\nRegistration required\n. For more inform
 ation\, please contact the branch at\n416-394-1000.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1ede64703c3363002bb5d5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Future-Proof Your Career With AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T193000
UID:6a1ef4a6caf9343600601358@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The job market is changing fast\, but AI can help candidates s
 tay ahead. This session explores how to use AI to identify skill gaps\, ex
 plore new roles\, and track industry trends. Participants will leave with 
 strategies to stay agile\, resilient\, and prepared for the future of work
 .
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1ef4a6caf9343600601358
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
